{"name":"Ascension","deep":true,"image":null,"mentions":460,"casual":{"lead":["In looksmaxxing slang, ascension means a marked rise in perceived attractiveness, often shown through before-and-after photos. Members post ascension plans, protocols and progress updates on looksmax.org.","The term is a label for an outcome, so there is no single treatment or study behind it. What people do in pursuit of it ranges from grooming and fitness to medical interventions."],"sections":[{"h":"How it works","paras":["There is no single mechanism. Members describe combining changes such as body-fat loss, skin, hair, dental or surgical work, and in some cases hormones, depending on the plan."],"subs":[]},{"h":"Risks and caveats","paras":["Risks depend entirely on the methods used. Some forum posts describe emotional outcomes: one thread title holds that ascension will not cure psychological issues."],"subs":[]}]},"gallery":[],"links":{"studies":[{"title":"Expression of flagella is coincident with uropathogenic Escherichia coli ascension to the upper urinary tract.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/17925449/","source":"Proceedings of the National Academy of Sciences of the United States of America","year":2007,"cites":338,"kind":null},{"title":"Bacterial vaginosis and its association with infertility, endometritis, and pelvic inflammatory disease.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/33091407/","source":"American journal of obstetrics and gynecology","year":2021,"cites":257,"kind":"Review"},{"title":"The dynamics of rapid sperm transport through the female genital tract: evidence from vaginal sonography of uterine peristalsis and hysterosalpingoscintigraphy.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/8671281/","source":"Human reproduction (Oxford, England)","year":1996,"cites":251,"kind":null},{"title":"Factors related to inflammation of the ovarian epithelium and risk of ovarian cancer.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/11021606/","source":"Epidemiology (Cambridge, Mass